Third-party components
----------------------

Ultralytics YOLO11 (AGPL-3.0) — https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics
    `models/onnx/detector.onnx` is fine-tuned from `yolo11n.pt`.

DINOv2 (Apache-2.0) — https://github.com/facebookresearch/dinov2
timm (Apache-2.0) — https://github.com/huggingface/pytorch-image-models
    `models/onnx/embedding.onnx` is fine-tuned from the timm weight tag
    `vit_base_patch14_dinov2.lvd142m`.

ONNX Runtime (MIT), OpenCV (Apache-2.0), FastAPI (MIT), Uvicorn (BSD-3-Clause),
httpx (BSD-3-Clause), orjson (Apache-2.0 / MIT), NumPy (BSD-3-Clause).


Training data
-------------

DogFaceNet — https://github.com/GuillaumeMougeot/DogFaceNet
    Identity embedding. The code is MIT; the images are described only as
    retrieved from the web, with no stated image licence.

Stanford Dogs — http://vision.stanford.edu/aditya86/ImageNetDogs/
    Detection. Derived from ImageNet, whose terms permit non-commercial
    research and educational use only.

DogReID-1553 (CC0 1.0) — https://doi.org/10.7910/DVN/LVTRLG
    Detection and identity embedding.

MPDD, Multi-pose Dog Dataset (CC BY 4.0) — https://doi.org/10.17632/v5j6m8dzhv.1
    Identity embedding.

COCO 2017 — https://cocodataset.org
    Detection. Annotations are CC BY 4.0; images carry their Flickr licences,
    some of them non-commercial.

Open Images V7 — https://storage.googleapis.com/openimages/web/index.html
    Detection (cats and dogs). Annotations are CC BY 4.0 (Google LLC); images
    are CC BY 2.0, with each author and Flickr page listed per image in the
    dataset's image CSV.

Oxford-IIIT Pet (CC BY-SA 4.0) — https://www.robots.ox.ac.uk/~vgg/data/pets/
    Detection (cats and dogs, boxed from the segmentation trimaps).

Cat Individual Images (CC BY 4.0) — https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/timost1234/cat-individuals
    Cat detection and identity embedding. Boxes are pseudo-labels from COCO
    YOLO11x.

Because of the training data terms above, the models are offered for
non-commercial research and personal use. This is a narrower grant than the
AGPL gives the code, and it is why this project is not offered for commercial
use.
